    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Safety\nIf you are sitting in an exit row\nand you cannot understand this\ncard or cannot see well enough\nto follow these instructions,\nplease tell a crew member.\nSicherheit\nSécurité\nSeguridad\nWenn Sie neben einem Ausgang sitzen und Sie verstehen\nkein Englisch, bitte verständigen Sie die Flugzeugbesatzung.\nSi vous êtes assis dans une rangée de sièges à côté d'une\nsortie et ne comprenez pas la langue anglaise, veuillez le dire\nà un membre de l'équipage.\nSi usted se encuentra sentado en una corrida de asientos\npróxima a una salida y no entiende el idioma Inglés como para\nseguir estas instrucciones por tavor avisele a una azafata.\nA320\nOverwater\nEmergency exits are often heavy, awkward to lift, push, pull,\nand maneuver when opening. Because of this, and for the\nsafety of all passengers, Federal Law requires that we only\nseat qualified passengers next to exits.\nIf you are sitting in an exit row, you may be asked to open the\nexit and assist our crew in the event of an emergency.\nPlease ask to be reseated if you:\n• Have a physical condition which may not be visible and\nwhich may prevent you from assisting.\n• Lack the strength, mobility, dexterity, in both arms and hands or\nlack the balance required to open the exit and assist our crew.\n• Do not think you could reach the exit, open it, and get out quickly.\n• Believe the physical exertion required to open the exit would\ninjure you.\n• Are hearing impaired and could not hear commands from our crew.\n• Lack sufficient visual capacity to assess outside conditions\nor performany necessary function without the assistance of\nvisual aids beyond eye glasses or contact lenses.\n• Are not able to give oral commands to others.\n• Do not understand the instructions in this brochure.\n• Have other responsibilities (such as a small child to care for)\nwhich would prevent you from helping.\n• Are less than 15 years old.\n• Do not wish to assist.\nFederal regulations require all passengers, regardless of\nwhere they are sitting or their physical condition, to\nreview this card, for their safety.\nFollow these instructions, the directions of crew\nmembers, and placarded signs.\nWhen finished reviewing this card please return it to the\nseat pocket for our next customer.\nUNITEDAIRLINES",
      "Do not use\n025818\nBenutzen Sie nicht...\nNe pas utiliser ...\nNo use...\nLife Rafts\n***$\n7945\nSchlauchboote\nCanot pneumatique\nBalsas salvavidas\n2\n3\nCA 380 10/98\nPrinted in the U.S.A.",
      "Take-off \u0026 landing\nNo smoking\nStart und Landung\nDécollage et atterissage\nDespegar y aterrizar\nRauchen verboten\nDéfense de fumer\nNo fumar\nBefore opening an exit,\nquickly look through a\nwindow to check outside\nfor the following:\nSmoke\nEmergency exits\n#*0\nNotausgänge\nSorties de secours\nSalidas de emergencia\nBB2 4\nIf smoke is so thick you can not see out,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nFire\nA\nIf there is fire outside the aircraft.\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nDebris/\nObstructions\nIf there is metal debris or obstructions,\ndirect passengers to other exits.\nDirect passengers away\nfrom aircraft.\nExit\n1*0\n57\nAusgang\nSortie\nSalida\nB\nA\nOxygen\n111\nSauerstoff\nOxygène\nOxigeno\n2\nCheck that the slide has properly\ninflated and is in good condition.\nUse handles to stabilize slide."
    ],
